  "critique": {
    "axis": "memorability",
    "evidence": "The provocative “Accuracy is the wrong question” thesis, cyan/red defense-lab palette, numbered ledger framing, and restrained monospace annotations give the screen a recognizable forensic-console identity across all viewports. However, most of the body resolves into familiar dark dashboard cards, standard charts, KPI tiles, and a conventional table; no single data visualization becomes a signature demo moment. Mobile further dilutes the idea into a long stack of generic panels.",
    "fix": "Create one unmistakable hero visualization that dramatizes the cost of optimizing accuracy—such as an interactive operating-threshold sweep linking false positives, fraud caught, money, and latency—and make it the screen’s dominant visual motif across desktop and mobile.",
